WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.810
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

00:04.810 --> 00:12.530
Asano hitogomi o nagamete coffee nondeiru
Watching a crowd in the morning, and drinking coffee

00:13.490 --> 00:21.500
Aseri nado naikano youni hitoni wa mieru daro
People must see me as if I don't have any worries

00:22.120 --> 00:29.960
lma menomae ni atomodori dekinai jikan ga
I know that the time I will never be able to get back

00:30.750 --> 00:38.260
Tashika ni nagareteru koto o watashi wa shitteru
Is moving in front of me

00:38.470 --> 00:47.480
Marude kyou shika nai toiu ikikata o shitemita toki
If I live like today is the last day of my life

00:47.770 --> 00:55.530
Saisho ni nani ga mieru darou
I wonder what I can see first

00:56.610 --> 01:00.830
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:01.290 --> 01:09.290
Sore ga donnani chiisana hikari demo ii
I don't care no matter how small the light is

01:09.790 --> 01:11.800
Sugata o misete hoshii
I just wish to see its shape

01:11.800 --> 01:16.010
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:16.680 --> 01:22.470
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.470 --> 01:22.680
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.680 --> 01:29.190
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
Sonna hito ni deaitai
Who I can tell my honest feelings to

01:29.190 --> 01:31.020
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology

01:39.380 --> 01:41.280
<i>All the way from</i>
<i>Tokyo by yourself?</i>

01:41.690 --> 01:42.850
<i>You're doing a good job.</i>

01:42.990 --> 01:44.680
<i>I'm going to see my mother.</i>

01:44.790 --> 01:45.950
<i>Your mother?</i>

01:46.130 --> 01:49.030
<i>Yes. We're going to live</i>
<i>together from now on.</i>

01:52.900 --> 01:55.130
<i>Oh, see, there she is.</i>

01:56.470 --> 01:58.270
<i>Mother!</i>

02:17.190 --> 02:21.700
Episode 12
Mermaid's Scar
(Part I)

02:23.740 --> 02:27.370
Winter, Two Years Later

03:26.530 --> 03:27.650
Mother.

03:43.140 --> 03:44.340
Good morning.

03:45.980 --> 03:46.950
Yukie.

03:48.680 --> 03:50.940
Where's your mother,
Young Master?

03:51.480 --> 03:53.140
She's still sleeping.

03:57.420 --> 03:59.150
Good morning, Masato.

03:59.490 --> 04:01.650
Oh, Ma'am,
good morning.

04:09.300 --> 04:11.790
Masato,
come over here.

04:23.920 --> 04:26.820
The story about the monster
that washed ashore?

04:27.520 --> 04:29.110
Oh, that.

04:29.890 --> 04:31.820
I think it was about
this time last year.

04:31.820 --> 04:33.920
A strange body washed ashore.

04:35.390 --> 04:36.380
Did you see it?

04:36.760 --> 04:39.660
I saw limbs that looked human...

04:39.730 --> 04:42.030
but the face was
like a disgusting fish.

04:42.300 --> 04:45.070
It was soon caught by a wave
and disappeared.

04:45.670 --> 04:48.070
I never figured out what it was.

04:51.980 --> 04:54.540
<i>We've come to this town</i>
<i>lead by a rumor, but...</i>

05:07.890 --> 05:10.520
Haven't you ever made tea before?

05:12.730 --> 05:13.360
Mana...

05:13.670 --> 05:15.000
have you done something again?

05:15.000 --> 05:16.060
Yuta!

05:17.200 --> 05:19.190
What kind of girl is she?

05:19.670 --> 05:20.710
She's unbelievable.

05:20.710 --> 05:21.900
She gets mad easily.

05:22.310 --> 05:23.100
I'm sorry.

05:23.410 --> 05:24.770
She's naive.

05:25.180 --> 05:27.440
Come on,
she's not a princess.

05:28.780 --> 05:29.800
Auntie.

05:30.350 --> 05:31.840
Oh, Yukie.

05:32.020 --> 05:33.510
We're in the middle of shopping.

05:34.350 --> 05:35.620
We need a little break.

05:36.560 --> 05:39.650
Oh, is he the boy
from the mansion?

05:40.160 --> 05:41.790
Yuta, that little boy.

05:42.560 --> 05:43.820
What about him?

05:44.000 --> 05:44.860
Remember...

05:44.860 --> 05:47.060
when I rode a train
for the first time.

05:47.870 --> 05:49.530
Oh, two years ago.

05:49.870 --> 05:51.670
We did pass this town then.

05:52.170 --> 05:54.640
You're still little, aren't you?

05:55.910 --> 05:57.400
What?
You know each other?

05:57.480 --> 05:58.740
Don't you remember us?

05:59.240 --> 06:01.510
You said you were going to
meet your mom.

06:05.120 --> 06:06.580
Are you happy?

06:10.120 --> 06:10.880
You are?

06:11.690 --> 06:12.710
That's good.

06:13.930 --> 06:17.260
Hey, isn't he going to school?

06:17.500 --> 06:20.020
It seems that his mother
hasn't registered him for school.

06:21.830 --> 06:22.960
She's...

06:23.500 --> 06:24.760
a little scary.

06:26.000 --> 06:27.440
See you, auntie.

06:30.040 --> 06:33.810
There's a strange rumor about
the lady who lives in the mansion...

06:34.180 --> 06:36.550
where Yukie works as a helper.

06:36.880 --> 06:37.780
A rumor?

06:38.250 --> 06:41.010
She was the second wife
to a wealthy, old man.

06:41.690 --> 06:43.850
A few years ago, I think...

06:44.390 --> 06:47.880
the yacht they were on
crashed into a motorboat.

06:48.160 --> 06:49.830
The husband died
in the accident and...

06:49.830 --> 06:53.700
she also died from severe burns
all over her body.

06:54.400 --> 06:56.130
But they say
she came back to life.

06:57.070 --> 06:58.370
Not only that...

06:58.370 --> 07:00.700
she disappeared from
the hospital the next day.

07:01.240 --> 07:03.240
And when she came back
to her house after a while...

07:03.240 --> 07:04.400
she was completely healed.

07:04.810 --> 07:07.180
My friend who was at
the hospital then said...

07:07.610 --> 07:11.840
there was no way she could heal
like that in such a short time.

07:12.780 --> 07:14.620
<i>A woman who came back to life...</i>

07:15.620 --> 07:17.820
<i>A strange body</i>
<i>that washed ashore...</i>

07:23.660 --> 07:26.760
<i>The wound is not healing...</i>

07:46.520 --> 07:48.850
Where did you hide
the mermaid flesh?!

07:48.950 --> 07:50.820
I don't know, I don't know!

07:51.260 --> 07:52.380
Ma'am!

07:55.430 --> 07:56.420
Stop right there!

08:12.210 --> 08:13.840
What's all this about?

08:29.090 --> 08:30.430
It should be OK.

08:30.860 --> 08:32.850
Your wound isn't
as deep as I thought.

08:33.500 --> 08:35.090
Did you say your name was Yuta?

08:35.330 --> 08:37.030
I'm glad you came.

08:37.200 --> 08:38.260
How is she?

08:38.670 --> 08:40.660
She seems calm now...

08:41.170 --> 08:42.230
but what now?

08:42.340 --> 08:43.670
Should we call the police?

08:43.740 --> 08:44.640
No!

08:46.010 --> 08:47.980
I don't want them to
take my mother away.

08:48.810 --> 08:52.480
Please don't tell anybody
about what happened today.

08:53.820 --> 08:55.120
Young Master...

08:58.060 --> 08:58.850
Hey.

08:59.690 --> 09:01.020
I'll go talk to her...

09:01.430 --> 09:03.720
and tell her not to be
so mean to her own kid.

09:11.140 --> 09:12.630
I came to see you.

09:13.410 --> 09:15.500
Who are you?

09:18.480 --> 09:19.810
Pretty interesting, isn't it?

09:20.880 --> 09:21.900
You...

09:23.010 --> 09:25.110
I ate mermaid flesh.

09:25.550 --> 09:27.110
I've been alive for 500 years.

09:27.790 --> 09:30.050
Most wounds heal instantly...

09:30.420 --> 09:33.980
and even if I die, I come back
to life in half a day or so.

09:34.890 --> 09:37.520
You ate mermaid flesh too,
didn't you?

09:38.300 --> 09:40.030
And I think you still
have some more.

09:43.230 --> 09:45.940
The monster that was floating
nearby in the ocean...

09:45.940 --> 09:47.940
That was the body
of a Deformed One.

09:47.940 --> 09:49.940
Who had eaten
mermaid flesh...

09:49.940 --> 09:51.700
and failed to become
immortal, wasn't it?

09:52.210 --> 09:54.270
Mermaid flesh is a deadly poison.

09:55.080 --> 09:58.280
Most humans either
die or become monsters.

10:05.160 --> 10:07.590
If what you say is true...

10:08.430 --> 10:09.450
Mother.

10:10.930 --> 10:12.290
What's going on?

10:12.600 --> 10:14.330
What's mermaid flesh?

10:16.330 --> 10:18.500
We'll talk when he's not around.

10:20.040 --> 10:22.010
Are you sure you'll be all right?

10:22.370 --> 10:24.210
Would you like me to
stay here for the night?

10:24.210 --> 10:25.910
Or you can come with me
if you want.

10:25.910 --> 10:27.000
Although it's just a bunkhouse.

10:27.280 --> 10:29.750
No. I'm OK.

10:30.520 --> 10:32.110
All right.
See you, then.

10:39.160 --> 10:41.020
<i>We have to do</i>
<i>something for him.</i>

10:42.630 --> 10:44.490
<i>Mermaid flesh is a poison?</i>

10:45.500 --> 10:47.930
<i>Not everyone</i>
<i>becomes immortal?</i>

10:48.630 --> 10:51.970
<i>Then am I going to die as well?</i>

10:53.970 --> 10:55.800
<i>I have to find it before I die.</i>

10:58.310 --> 10:59.710
<i>The mermaid flesh...</i>

11:03.970 --> 11:13.980
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest

11:20.970 --> 11:22.800
You're going to quit your job?

11:23.000 --> 11:23.730
Yeah.

11:25.440 --> 11:27.130
Wow, it's beautiful!

11:27.440 --> 11:29.670
Oh, so you're getting married.

11:30.110 --> 11:31.630
Congratulations.

11:33.080 --> 11:34.480
I somehow managed.

11:36.780 --> 11:39.050
Oh, good for you.

11:39.880 --> 11:42.190
I feel sorry for the boy
at the mansion, though.

11:42.190 --> 11:44.120
I feel like I'm walking out on him.

11:44.860 --> 11:46.850
You're a kind-hearted woman,
Yukie.

11:47.290 --> 11:48.880
You'll make a wonderful wife.

11:50.330 --> 11:51.520
Thank you.

11:52.560 --> 11:56.060
Yuta, please keep an eye on him.

11:56.470 --> 11:58.200
Yeah, leave it to me.

11:58.800 --> 12:00.030
Goodbye, then.

12:00.540 --> 12:01.530
Goodbye.

12:11.680 --> 12:13.120
One of us?

12:13.120 --> 12:15.640
Are you talking about that woman
who came back to life?

12:15.820 --> 12:19.190
I know she might be
a little hard to deal with, but...

12:20.260 --> 12:21.730
You want to take her along?

12:23.130 --> 12:25.390
I don't think she's the type
who'd happily come with us.

12:26.400 --> 12:29.760
But, in any case,
we can't leave the boy like this.

12:40.510 --> 12:43.970
Oh, so you are leaving.

12:44.650 --> 12:47.310
But I'm happy for you.
All the best to you.

12:47.750 --> 12:50.240
Yes, thank you very much.

13:02.530 --> 13:03.360
Young Master.

13:03.770 --> 13:04.860
Young Master Masato.

13:10.610 --> 13:11.580
Young Master.

13:14.680 --> 13:15.610
Yukie...

13:16.250 --> 13:17.610
You're leaving.

13:18.380 --> 13:19.540
Were you listening?

13:20.850 --> 13:21.820
I'm sorry.

13:22.090 --> 13:24.520
I wish I could stay
with you longer, but...

13:25.460 --> 13:26.510
Look.

13:28.890 --> 13:30.360
I want you to try this.

13:41.110 --> 13:42.800
What is it?

14:17.110 --> 14:17.600
Masato!

14:23.950 --> 14:25.180
Deformed One?

14:42.430 --> 14:43.560
Yuta!

14:49.840 --> 14:50.570
Mana!

14:52.210 --> 14:53.230
I'm OK.

14:53.480 --> 14:54.980
Take the kid and
get out of here!

14:54.980 --> 14:56.210
Hey, get up!

14:57.450 --> 14:59.110
You're not getting away!

15:02.890 --> 15:03.980
What are you doing?

15:05.990 --> 15:07.050
Stop!

15:09.190 --> 15:10.490
Masato...

15:28.250 --> 15:30.240
Stay here.
I'm going back there.

15:31.080 --> 15:32.570
You're hurt.

15:33.350 --> 15:34.480
It's nothing.

15:42.230 --> 15:43.320
You're...

16:41.790 --> 16:42.910
<i>Thank you.</i>

16:46.020 --> 16:47.050
Yukie...

16:52.700 --> 16:54.600
Hey, what does all this mean?

16:54.770 --> 16:56.170
Why has Yukie!

16:56.470 --> 16:57.560
Answer me!

16:58.670 --> 17:02.330
He...in my place...

17:02.670 --> 17:03.940
Yukie...

17:04.240 --> 17:05.710
by him...

17:10.650 --> 17:14.410
Are you sure you have a poison
to kill Deformed Ones?

17:14.690 --> 17:15.950
We're almost there.

17:17.620 --> 17:21.060
Don't be fooled by him.

17:21.960 --> 17:27.090
I met Masato for the first time...

17:27.830 --> 17:33.170
on the day after the air raid
on Tokyo during the Pacific War.

17:38.340 --> 17:40.830
My husband had been killed
in the war long before that...

17:42.010 --> 17:44.950
and our only son,
who had just turned eight...

17:44.950 --> 17:46.420
was also killed in the raid.

17:47.350 --> 17:51.880
I was all alone and
no longer had the will to survive.

17:53.220 --> 17:56.960
That's when he...

18:02.930 --> 18:05.300
<i>Nice lady, have some.</i>

18:05.840 --> 18:07.000
He did?

18:11.140 --> 18:13.130
This is my secret hiding place.

18:13.210 --> 18:15.080
Forget the hiding place.
Hurry up and get the poison!

18:15.480 --> 18:17.470
You don't have to fret.

18:18.250 --> 18:21.120
Since then...

18:21.120 --> 18:26.920
he took good care of me.

18:28.390 --> 18:34.960
I felt like my dead son
had come back to me...

18:35.970 --> 18:39.460
and we started living
like a true mother and son.

18:40.840 --> 18:45.210
But, no matter how many years
passed, he didn't grow up.

18:46.110 --> 18:49.440
And my body healed instantly
whenever I got hurt.

18:50.180 --> 18:52.050
I was so scared, and...

18:52.820 --> 18:55.450
<i>What are you?</i>

18:57.460 --> 19:02.120
He said he'd eaten
mermaid flesh in the past.

19:02.690 --> 19:04.290
And that he gave it to me as well.

19:06.060 --> 19:08.290
With a child who never grew up...

19:08.870 --> 19:11.230
I couldn't stay in one place
for even three years.

19:12.770 --> 19:16.330
In my desperation,
I tried strangling him to death...

19:17.310 --> 19:19.000
but he came back to life.

19:21.150 --> 19:24.670
I fled from him and got married.

19:25.680 --> 19:28.850
I was finally able to live like
a normal human being, but...

19:31.220 --> 19:34.490
he probably found a newspaper
article about the yacht crash...

19:35.860 --> 19:37.620
and he came after me.

19:37.860 --> 19:39.350
<i>Mother.</i>

19:40.060 --> 19:44.590
I thought I could never free myself
from him as long as I was alive.

19:44.970 --> 19:48.930
I almost gave up, but...

19:49.840 --> 19:53.280
It started taking
more and more time...

19:54.180 --> 19:57.480
for my wounds to heal.

19:57.620 --> 20:00.240
So you've come to need
more mermaid flesh.

20:00.790 --> 20:03.650
I pressed him
many times to tell me.

20:03.850 --> 20:05.960
<i>Where did you hide</i>
<i>the mermaid flesh?!</i>

20:05.960 --> 20:07.720
<i>I don't know, I don't know!</i>

20:08.360 --> 20:10.790
And it sometimes lead to...

20:12.800 --> 20:14.730
Then...

20:16.270 --> 20:17.170
he...

20:18.200 --> 20:19.100
<i>Fine...</i>

20:19.600 --> 20:22.100
<i>I'll find a replacement again.</i>

20:23.640 --> 20:27.580
I don't care about
myself anymore.

20:28.110 --> 20:31.480
But I have to take...

20:31.480 --> 20:35.350
the mermaid flesh
away from him.

20:39.060 --> 20:45.090
Or, he'll repeat the same thing
over and over again.

20:50.070 --> 20:50.860
Hey...

20:51.470 --> 20:52.270
Hey!

20:52.840 --> 20:53.830
Hey!

20:55.110 --> 20:58.340
You know, your friend
and my mother...

20:58.340 --> 21:00.370
might already be dead by now.

21:00.680 --> 21:03.010
Stop fooling around.
Hurry up and get the poison!

21:05.380 --> 21:07.440
The wound's gone...
You!

21:15.530 --> 21:17.620
It's called a stun gun.

21:18.060 --> 21:19.760
Did you know?

21:20.970 --> 21:23.460
<i>He can't live alone.</i>

21:24.140 --> 21:27.870
<i>There probably were</i>
<i>women before me...</i>

21:28.540 --> 21:30.410
<i>whom he fed mermaid flesh to...</i>

21:30.410 --> 21:32.900
<i>and forced to become</i>
<i>his companion.</i>

21:34.310 --> 21:36.910
<i>And there will be</i>
<i>more after me...</i>

21:37.880 --> 21:38.750
Mana.

21:40.890 --> 21:41.720
Mana!

21:42.250 --> 21:44.220
Mana!!

21:46.790 --> 21:48.620
Yu...ta...

21:51.630 --> 21:52.860
Yuta...

21:56.670 --> 22:00.570
He's an obstacle.

22:25.070 --> 22:33.580
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

22:34.950 --> 22:43.460
ltsumade kakaruno to anata wa warau kedo
"How long does it take?" You smiled at me

22:44.920 --> 22:53.810
Dorekurai oboete iru hidoku naki nagara
How much do you remember? I cried hard

22:54.850 --> 23:04.360
Dorekurai oboete iru anokoto to ieba
How much do you remember if I talk about "that thing"?

23:09.450 --> 23:18.460
ltsumademo mada utsumuite
I still look down

23:19.420 --> 23:27.920
Tobikoe rarenai mizutamari
I can't jump over the puddle

23:29.050 --> 23:38.560
Wakaranakunaru moshikasuruto
I'm confused

23:38.890 --> 23:48.400
Kawarenai no wa watashi dake kana
Maybe I'm the only one who still can't change

23:53.370 --> 24:02.880
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

24:06.660 --> 24:09.100
Masato, do you know
what you've done to Yukie?

24:09.970 --> 24:12.440
She was always so kind to you!

24:13.770 --> 24:17.310
I know how tough
it is to live alone.

24:18.710 --> 24:22.150
But you shouldn't feed
mermaid flesh to others!

24:23.610 --> 24:25.380
I'll never forgive you.

24:25.950 --> 24:27.210
Return Mana to me!

24:28.390 --> 24:28.980
Next, Last Episode,
"Mermaid's Scar", Part II.

24:28.980 --> 24:32.960
Last Episode
Mermaid's Scar
(Part II)
Next, Last Episode,
"Mermaid's Scar", Part II.

24:32.960 --> 24:34.980
Next Episode
Last Episode
Mermaid's Scar
